description:
Filed by s537b (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-13, s540 resume) from #4461's predicted-vs-actual comparison: App/Cpan.pm's five predicted block-extent sites (lines 676, 1586-1589, each `my $x;` at the top of a `BEGIN { ... sub NAME { ... } ... }` with a string eval in a sub of the block) did not move because the file is refused on BOTH trees (main 23f0f917 and the s537b tree) with the same message.  Pre-existing; LOUD (a whole-file refusal, not a silent wrong).

REPRODUCER (perl 5.40.3 prints `3`; PCL: "Transpile failed: Parser2 TODO: promoted cell $d__file__0 never registered for eval capture"):

    BEGIN {
      my $d = 3;
      sub g { $d }
      my $e = eval '1';
    }
    print g(), "\n";

Same for an END body (`END { my $d = 4; sub g { $d } my $e = eval '$d + 1'; print g(), " $e\n" }` -- perl `4 5`) and for an eval inside a sub of the block (`BEGIN { my $n = 0; sub bump { ++$n } sub peek { eval '$n' } }` -- perl prints the empty string: the eval runs after BEGIN's pad is gone, "Variable is not available").  Without the string eval the shape works (`BEGIN { my $d = 3; sub g { $d } } print g()` -> 3 on both).

MECHANISM (read, not fixed): `_promote_captured` promotes `$d` (a named sub in the block captures it) and, because a string eval follows the declaration, arms the M-F backstop `_pending_eval_caps` -- the promise that the decl LOWERS through `_lower_decl_list`'s renamed-cell branch, where `_eval_reach_promoted` (s537b) registers the alias or the per-site pair and clears the flag.  A BEGIN / END body is lowered through the v1 bridge (s533c: "a 15-line bridge for blocks v1 still compiles, BEGIN/END bodies"), so the native decl branch never runs and the end-of-parse check dies on the pending name.  Fix direction: the bridge either lowers the body's declarations natively (C2's next statement kinds, the codegen review's step 1d) or registers the pending cells itself; the eval-pair rule for a BLOCK extent is the per-site pair (#4461), and a sub body's eval after the block is perl's "not available" rule (DECIDED s504c's note).

POPULATION: App/Cpan.pm (core lib) is the one file of the wide list (2,053 files) whose refusal is this message (s537b's scan.log: 5 of the 22 block-extent alias sites).
